'''Meditation Cat''' is a [[:Category:Special Cats|Special Cat]] that can be obtained from the [[Download Celebration! (Event Gacha)|Download Celebration!]] Event Gacha. It was added to [[Nyanko Daisensou|BCJP]] in [[Version 11.10 Update|Version 11.10]], and [[The Battle Cats|BCEN]] in [[Version 13.6 Update|Version 13.6]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 689
|rarity = EX
|name1 = Meditation Cat
|name2 = Paragon Cat
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Paragon Cat''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
This unit is similar to [[Battle Items#Sniper the Cat|Sniper the Cat]] in that it sits behind the [[Cat Base]] and knocks back enemies. The differences are that Paragon Cat has much lower range and is ineffective against [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] enemies and [[:Category:Enemies with Knockback Immunity|Knockback-immune enemies]]. While not entirely useless on stages featuring [[:Category:Long Distance Enemies|Long Distance attacks]], [[:Category:Wave Attack Enemies|Wave]] [[:Category:Mini-Wave Enemies|Attacks]], or [[:Category:Surge Attack Enemies|Surge]] [[:Category:Mini-Surge Enemies|Attacks]], using Paragon Cat on said stages is risky since they can be sniped if the enemies are too close to the Cat Base. [[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|Wave Shields]] can at least help alleviate the risk on Wave stages.

Due to how units get sent out, it can only hit enemies that are up to '''500px''' away from the Cat Base, meaning it will be useless against enemies with a range higher than 500, like [[Camelle]] and his variants. It also fares very poorly on [[Duel Stages Challenge|Duel Stages]] and [[Tag Arena Challenge|Tag Arena stages]], or other levels where there is a [[Restriction Stage|restriction]] on how many Cat Units can be sent out, since it will not contribute to the fight for the most part and enemies likely won't kill it to make room for more units.

That being said, it works very well on stages where enemies have to be fought close to the Cat Base, such as due to a [[Doge Base (Enemy Base)|Doge Base]] or [[Surge Base (Enemy Base)|Surge Base]], or stages with very few peons to get in the way, like [[Kugel Schreiber]]. It also excels in [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]]-heavy stages, where it can easily knock away any threatening Zombies that [[Burrow]] close to your base. In particular, it can act as a hard counter to [[Big Sal]], capable of stunlocking one indefinitely on its own. It pairs exceptionally with the default [[Cat Cannon]] or a [[:Category:Waver-class Cats|Wave Attacker]] to clear weak enemies so it doesn't waste an attack.

There is not much point stacking this cat, since most enemies will be knocked out of its range, which will cause their attacks to sync.

