==Trivia==
*Meditation Cat was originally obtainable from the [[10th Memorial (Event Gacha)|10th Memorial]] Event Gacha during the [[Anniversary/10th Year|10th Anniversary]] celebration event.
*Meditation Cat may be based on the idiom ''ishi no ue ni mo sannen'' (石の上にも三年, "three years on a stone"), which is to say that no matter how difficult something is, it can eventually be achieved with enough patience.
*Meditation Cat's Japanese description begins in the form of ''Nazokake'' (謎掛け), a word game where you find the similarity between two named things.
*The marking on Meditation Cat's stone is 十, the Japanese word for 10.
*This is actually [[PONOS Corporation|PONOS]]' second take on a completely unmoving "base defender" unit. The first was [https://seesaawiki.jp/urugege/d/%C0%E9%C7%AF%A4%CB%B0%EC%CA%E2%CA%E2%A4%AF%C4%BB The Bird That Takes One Step a Millennium], one of the most prevalently used [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare]] units in [[Yuru-i GeGeGe no Kitarou: Youkai Dotabata Daisensou|YuruGeGe]]. While this Uber had a blind spot and took nearly 10 minutes to recharge, it also had exceptional damage (102,000 at level 30) and reach (450~2700), Area Attack, and a cost of only 1,002, making it extremely valuable as a stackable base defender in levels with non-timed bosses, or to be saved up like the [[Cat Cannon]] until a group of dangerous enemies appeared, especially in levels that rushed players with such enemies at the beginning. Perhaps to avoid creating such a versatile unit again, Meditation Cat is given many disadvantages that its predecessor lacked, namely Single Attack and an extremely low damage output that makes it almost pointless to stack.
*The [[Ototo Corps#Iron Wall|Iron Wall Cat]], Meditation Cat, [[Mamoluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Mamolan Pasalan]], and [[Cheetah Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Cheetah Cat]] are the only units with 0 speed.
**The Iron Wall Cat, Meditation Cat, and Mamolan Pasalan are also the only non-[[Conjure|conjured]] units to be Immune to Boss Shockwaves.

